All,

After my ASIC presentation on the limits of PE and lessons learned from the=
 irrigation application these last few years Chris Menno of Stahlman Englan=
d (irrigation contractor) approached Brian and me.  He was one of the earli=
er adopters of PE and has actively sought to convert golf projects to PE.

We discussed "Polygate" in Florida and the occasion where a contractor in a=
n effort to bait and switch a PVC system with PE had bought DR17 pipe assum=
ing he could get it approved.  That would be Paul Cope of Quality Grassing.=
  Chris Menno is familiar with this debacle.  It turns out that using the P=
E industry's own method as presented on the PPI website and the consultant'=
s system design parameters DR 17 could not be shown to be adequate.  The pa=
rameters are probably typical of any modern golf irrigation system in the s=
un belt.  Cope had no luck with the city engineer and ended up moving the D=
R 17 pipe on to a different unsuspecting owner.

I told him that others attribute the use of DR 17 on golf projects in Flori=
da to him and Zack.  He said that was back in a time when times were tough =
and he had to.  He seemed not to be phased by what he said.  That doing the=
 right thing was subordinate to his financial success.

It would seem that the integrity of the irrigation contractor corps is situ=
ational.

It is a shame that anyone would care what a contractor had to say about sys=
tem design choices related to long term performance.

J

=3D

--_000_9B7E2735CEC37E4D9137A9548F21D78372545FCA26MAIL_
